tleBot3 Navigation","Robotics & Reinforcement Learning","2022-03",[18,19,20,21],"ROS","TensorFlow","Python","Gazebo","Seeded a DQN with an Artificial Potential Field controller to dramatically cut training time for autonomous robot navigation in Gazebo.",false,{},"src/content/projects/apf-dqn.md","c5dfd0e2aa221506",{"html":28,"metadata":29},"",{"headings":30,"localImagePaths":31,"remoteImagePaths":32,"frontmatter":33,"imagePaths":36},[],[],[],{"title":14,"category":15,"date":16,"techStack":34,"description":22,"featured":23,"links":35},[18,19,20,21],{},[],"apf-dqn.md","legal-rag",{"id":38,"data":40,"filePath":54,"digest":55,"rendered":56,"legacyId":65},{"title":41,"category":42,"date":43,"techStack":44,"description":50,"summary":51,"featured":52,"links":53},"Legal Knowledge Graph RAG System","Generative AI & NLP","2025-11",[20,45,46,47,48,49],"Neo4j","Graphiti","Gemini","Pydantic","LangChain","A production-grade RAG assistant for immigration case law that outperforms standard retrieval by 15–17% using a 264K-node knowledge graph.","Built an end-to-end legal AI assistant that combines a Neo4j knowledge graph (264K nodes, 506K relationships) with Gemini 2.5 Flash to answer immigration case law questions. Pydantic-driven structured extraction turns raw court opinions into a typed graph — no hallucinated schema, no brittle parsing. Outperforms NaiveRAG and CBR-RAG by 15–17% on faithfulness, with a hybrid retrieval pipeline that blends vector search with Cypher-based multi-hop graph traversal.",true,{},"src/content/projects/legal-rag.md","e80e18e82c9cdfe6",{"html":28,"metadata":57},{"headings":58,"localImagePaths":59,"remoteImagePaths":60,"frontmatter":61,"imagePaths":64},[],[],[],{"title":41,"category":42,"date":43,"techStack":62,"description":50,"summary":51,"featured":52,"links":63},[20,45,46,47,48,49],{},[],"legal-rag.md","dna-regions",{"id":66,"data":68,"filePath":77,"digest":78,"rendered":79,"legacyId":88},{"title":69,"category":70,"date":71,"techStack":72,"description":75,"featured":23,"links":76},"CpG Island Detection in DNA Sequences","Algorithms & Foundations","2020-09",[20,73,74],"Divide and Conquer","Bioinformatics","Modified max-subarray algorithm that locates CpG nucleotide islands in mammalian DNA — a divide-and-conquer solution to a bioinformatics search problem.",{},"src/content/projects/dna-regions.md","8f7b4e004d651901",{"html":28,"metadata":80},{"headings":81,"localImagePaths":82,"remoteImagePaths":83,"frontmatter":84,"imagePaths":87},[],[],[],{"title":69,"category":70,"date":71,"techStack":85,"description":75,"featured":23,"links":86},[20,73,74],{},[],"dna-regions.md","load-forecasting",{"id":89,"data":91,"filePath":100,"digest":101,"rendered":102,"legacyId":111},{"title":92,"category":42,"date":93,"techStack":94,"description":98,"featured":23,"links":99},"Short-term Residential Load Forecasting","2021-03",[19,95,96,97],"Transformers","LSTM","Deep Q-Network","Benchmarked Transformers, LSTMs, and RL agents for household energy consumption forecasting — comparing architectures head-to-head on real load data.",{},"src/content/projects/load-forecasting.md","b714e99bd06cab04",{"html":28,"metadata":103},{"headings":104,"localImagePaths":105,"remoteImagePaths":106,"frontmatter":107,"imagePaths":110},[],[],[],{"title":92,"category":42,"date":93,"techStack":108,"description":98,"featured":23,"links":109},[19,95,96,97],{},[],"load-forecasting.md","parallel-interleave",{"id":112,"data":114,"filePath":126,"digest":127,"rendered":128,"legacyId":137},{"title":115,"category":116,"date":117,"techStack":118,"description":123,"summary":124,"featured":52,"links":125},"Parallel Interleave for MEC Decomposition","Systems / Hardware / Formal Methods","2026-01",[119,20,120,121,122],"C++","Storm","perf","Valgrind","Parallelized a core algorithm in the Storm probabilistic model checker, achieving 2–5x speedup on the QVBS benchmark suite.","Reimplemented the Interleave algorithm for Maximal End Component decomposition in Storm — a state-of-the-art probabilistic model checker — with parallel execution. Hit 2–5x speedup over the sequential baseline across the full QVBS benchmark suite. Built a profiling pipeline from scratch: perf with DWARF call-graphs at 997 Hz, Valgrind instrumentation, flamegraph generation, and C++ template symbol demangling to make profilers actually see the right entry points.",{},"src/content/projects/parallel-interleave.md","2841f1c7b3578b82",{"html":28,"metadata":129},{"headings":130,"localImagePaths":131,"remoteImagePaths":132,"frontmatter":133,"imagePaths":136},[],[],[],{"title":115,"category":116,"date":117,"techStack":134,"description":123,"summary":124,"featured":52,"links":135},[119,20,120,121,122],{},[],"parallel-interleave.md","optimal-seam",{"id":138,"data":140,"filePath":148,"digest":149,"rendered":150,"legacyId":159},{"title":141,"category":70,"date":142,"techStack":143,"description":146,"featured":23,"links":147},"Optimal Seam Finding","2020-11",[20,144,145],"Dynamic Programming","Image Processing","Dynamic programming algorithm for content-aware image resizing — finds minimal-energy seams so cropped images keep their visual proportions.",{},"src/content/projects/optimal-seam.md","36266d3371ee6893",{"html":28,"metadata":151},{"headings":152,"localImagePaths":153,"remoteImagePaths":154,"frontmatter":155,"imagePaths":158},[],[],[],{"title":141,"category":70,"date":142,"techStack":156,"description":146,"featured":23,"links":157},[20,144,145],{},[],"optimal-seam.md","french-gpt3",{"id":160,"data":162,"filePath":171,"digest":172,"rendered":173,"legacyId":182},{"title":163,"category":42,"date":164,"techStack":165,"description":169,"featured":23,"links":170},"Fine-tuned French GPT-3 Chatbot","2021-11",[166,167,168,20],"OpenAI API","GPT-3","Flask","A web app for fine-tuned French language generation with GPT-3, letting users retrain the model on their own datasets.",{},"src/content/projects/french-gpt3.md","f8557d10dc2c4247",{"html":28,"metadata":174},{"headings":175,"localImagePaths":176,"remoteImagePaths":177,"frontmatter":178,"imagePaths":181},[],[],[],{"title":163,"category":42,"date":164,"techStack":179,"description":169,"featured":23,"links":180},[166,167,168,20],{},[],"french-gpt3.md","popsign",{"id":183,"data":185,"filePath":195,"digest":196,"rendered":197,"legacyId":206},{"title":186,"category":42,"date":187,"techStack":188,"description":192,"summary":193,"featured":52,"links":194},"PopSign: AI Storybooks for ASL Learning","2025-10",[20,47,189,190,191],"Sentence-BERT","spaCy","Embedding-Gemma","A constrained generative pipeline that writes ASL children's stories with zero lexical errors and auto-grades them across Fountas-Pinnell reading levels.","Designed a generative AI pipeline that authors ASL-constrained children's stories using Gemini — with a custom validation framework that drove lexical constraint violations to zero. Built an NLP evaluation system using Sentence-BERT, spaCy, and readability metrics to auto-classify story difficulty across Fountas-Pinnell levels A–Z, enabling data-driven curriculum design. An embedding-based vocabulary sampler (Embedding-Gemma) generates semantically coherent, level-appropriate word sets for each story.",{},"src/content/projects/popsign.md","37e7fa3caec1217f",{"html":28,"metadata":198},{"headings":199,"localImagePaths":200,"remoteImagePaths":201,"frontmatter":202,"imagePaths":205},[],[],[],{"title":186,"category":42,"date":187,"techStack":203,"description":192,"summary":193,"featured":52,"links":204},[20,47,189,190,191],{},[],"popsign.md","pid-controller",{"id":207,"data":209,"filePath":218,"digest":219,"rendered":220,"legacyId":229},{"title":210,"category":15,"date":211,"techStack":212,"description":216,"featured":23,"links":217},"Quadcopter PID Controller","2021-02",[20,213,214,215],"Control Systems","PID","Robotics","Designed and tuned a PID controller for stable quadcopter flight — classical control, precisely calibrated.",{},"src/content/projects/pid-controller.md","e47b5c95b